# Agent descriptions

The YAML `description` field is how other agents decide to dispatch this
one. Write only:

- **When to use** — trigger phrases, slash commands, and situations
- **When not to use** — jobs this agent must not take

Start with `Use when` or `Use proactively when`. Follow with `Do not` or
`Never` for the negative.

Omit everything else from `description`: role titles, architecture, tool
lists, I/O, loop counts, and body-section content. Those belong in Charter
and later headings.

| Excuse | Reality |
| --- | --- |
| "Lead with what the agent is" | Other agents route on when/when-not, not job titles. |
| "A one-line summary helps humans" | Humans read the agent file. Description is a dispatch signal. |
